questions.scenario:
You are debugging a production issue where an order fulfillment workflow fails silently. When a downstream inventory service call fails, the database status for the order is expected to transition to `FAILED`. Instead, the client receives an HTTP 500 error, and the transaction is aborted. You inspect the following Spring service code:

java
@Service
public class OrderWorkflowService {

    @Autowired
    private InventoryServiceClient inventoryClient;
    @Autowired
    private OrderRepository orderRepository;

    @Transactional
    public void processOrder(Long orderId) {
        Order order = orderRepository.findById(orderId).orElseThrow();
        order.setStatus(OrderStatus.PROCESSING);
        orderRepository.save(order);

        try {
            inventoryClient.reserveStock(order);
        } catch (InventoryException ex) {
            // Attempt to gracefully record failure in DB
            order.setStatus(OrderStatus.FAILED);
            order.setFailureReason(ex.getMessage());
            orderRepository.save(order);
        }
    }
}

@Service
public class InventoryServiceClient {
    @Transactional(propagation = Propagation.REQUIRED)
    public void reserveStock(Order order) {
        // RPC call to external service fails
        throw new InventoryException("Insufficient inventory"); // Subclass of RuntimeException
    }
}

